    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `checkDigit` as a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`, following the existing derived-field pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` property to the `Owner` schema (integer, 0\u20139, `readOnly`), which regenerates the `OwnerDto` with a `checkDigit` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(checkDigit(owner))\")` and a `checkDigit(Owner)` default method implementing the standard Luhn algorithm over the digits in `customerCode` (returns `null` when the code is absent, mirroring `membershipNumber`).\n\nBecause the mapper drives both the create and read (`GET /api/owners/{id}`) responses, the field is populated consistently. The acceptance test `coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` \u2014 which recomputes Luhn from the returned `customerCode` and asserts the exact digit \u2014 passes, and the full suite is green.",
